[not-pure] Error: `apply` is declared `pure`, so it cannot call a function held in a value
   ╭─[ example.vaab:1:61 ]
   │
 1 │ pure to apply(f: to(Int) returns Int, n: Int) returns Int = f(n)
   │                                                       ─┬─   ──┬─  
   │                                                        │      ╰─── this calls a function held in a value
   │                                                        │          
   │                                                        ╰────────── `apply` is declared `pure` here
   │ 
   │ Help: call a function declared with `pure to` by name instead, since a function held in a value carries no record of whether it is `pure`
